{
  "title": "Acceptance P4a-1: an acceptance run gives one engine-checked verdict per requirement unit of the epic's intent",
  "body": "## Problem\nPart of M6.5, Epic P (#855), slice P4a-1.\n\nEvery epic ends with an acceptance ticket (docs/ISSUES.md), and the orchestrator runs each of them by hand. The factory can't run one. Its pieces exist since #915, but only for the verifier:\n\n- **The landed covering-test mechanism is verifier-shaped** (`src/pipeline/covering-tests.ts`):\n  - `selectCoveringTests(verify: Verify)` (:27-42) takes requests only from sandbox-blocked `Verify` criteria, with at most 3 per criterion and 10 per round.\n  - `coveringTestCommand` (:45-95) refuses a `retry_files` template containing `--` (:63-64). It checks containment (`validRetryFiles`, :65) and that the file is tracked at the verified SHA (literal-pathspec `ls-tree`, :70-85).\n  - `runCoveringTests(ctx, verify, sha, checkHead)` (:123-201) runs each test in its own `gates` stage, saving the result before the handle is cleared.\n  - `coveringTestRefusal` (:97-120) accepts only the run's own fresh JUnit testcase evidence (`readCoveringJUnit`, `src/gates/junit.ts:198-243`): the requested file and full name, no failure, error or skipped child, at the exact SHA, with tracked files unchanged.\n  - The engine computes its succeeded-stage list inline (`src/pipeline/engine.ts:2229-2234`).\n- **Citations are structured.** `applyGateEvidence` (`src/pipeline/gate-evidence.ts:248-323`) accepts only structured citations it checks against its own records (`citationRefusal`, :223-245), and writes the evidence text itself (`coveringCitation`, :160-161).\n- **Nothing else in the run model fits:**\n  - `insertRun` (`src/db/store.ts:1439-1491`) creates a run with no `state_json`, and the engine builds the initial state on first pickup (`src/pipeline/context.ts:395-400`), where an older engine defaults to `build`.\n  - A `NeedsHumanError` with a worktree reaches draft-PR delivery (`engine.ts:495-512`).\n  - Ordinary prepare allocates a branch, looks up PRs and runs baseline gates (`src/git/repos.ts:413-440`, `engine.ts:684-761`).\n  - Stage caching covers only gates, audit and review in the loop phase (`context.ts:561-567`).\n  - Flows, phases and stage names are closed unions: `Run.flow` (`src/core/types.ts:129`), `StageName` (:43-56), `Phase` (`context.ts:74`), and the `ReportInput.state` `Pick` (`src/pipeline/report.ts:74-91`).\n\n## Invariant\n- **What is assessed.** An acceptance run assesses exactly the intent units the engine resolved, before any model call, from trusted text snapshotted at creation.\n  - Each unit has a stable id. A unit is a whole source unit: a list item, a paragraph, a blockquote paragraph or a table cell.\n  - Each unit has an evidence class, `behaviour` (the default) or `docs`, fixed by trusted ticket grammar during resolution. Model output can't change it.\n- **When a unit is `met`.**\n  - Every evidence item cited for it verifies in the engine's own records at the checked SHA.\n  - For a test, verification is #915's `coveringTestRefusal` returning nothing, unchanged.\n  - For a file, verification is #915's containment check followed by its SHA and tracked-membership check, both unchanged.\n  - At least one cited test verifies. Only a unit whose persisted class is `docs` may instead rest on at least one verified file matching the base commit's `[gates] docs`.\n- **When a run passes.** Every unit is assessed exactly once, and every unit is `met`.\n- **Publication.** No acceptance run publishes anything: no branch push, PR or comment, on any release, before or after a rollback. Existing lifecycle labels and fixed-text comments are the only exception (P4a-2).\n\n## Requirements\n1. **One shared covering-test primitive.** Extract it from `covering-tests.ts` without changing verifier behaviour.\n   - `selectCoveringRequests(items: Test[][])`: the 3-per-item and 10-per-round caps, and their reasons. `selectCoveringTests(verify)` becomes a wrapper over it.\n   - `runCoveringRequests(ctx, items, sha, checkHead)`: the body of `runCoveringTests`. `runCoveringTests` becomes a wrapper.\n   - **Validation order is preserved.** `coveringTestCommand` validates in this order today:\n     1. the retry configuration (:46-55);\n     2. the `--` refusal (:56-64);\n     3. containment (`validRetryFiles`, :65);\n     4. the test-file pattern (:66);\n     5. the name (:67-68);\n     6. SHA validity (:69);\n     7. tracked membership (literal-pathspec `ls-tree`, :70-85).\n\n     Containment stays where it is, at :65. Only the last two steps are extracted, as `trackedAtShaRefusal(file, cwd, sha)`, returning the same reasons. `coveringTestCommand` calls it at the same point, so every refusal's precedence, including the test-file and name checks between them, is unchanged.\n   - **Ordinary file citations** compose the two checks: `validRetryFiles([file], cwd)` (containment) first, then `trackedAtShaRefusal`, as `citedFileRefusal(file, cwd, sha)`.\n   - `succeededCoveringStages(ctx)`: the filter from `engine.ts:2229-2234`, used by the verify path and by acceptance.\n   - `coveringTestRefusal` and `coveringTestCommand` (including the `--` refusal) are reused unchanged.\n   - An acceptance run is round 0 throughout, so the per-round cap of 10 is its per-run cap.\n2. **Types and state.**\n   - `\"acceptance\"` joins `RunState.flow` and `Run.flow`. `\"accept\"` joins `Phase` and `StageName`.\n   - `RunState.acceptance` holds:\n     - the snapshot (ticket and parent bodies, numbers, authors, editors);\n     - the checked SHA;\n     - the resolved manifest;\n     - `setupDone`;\n     - the model output;\n     - the outcome.\n\n     `acceptance` joins `ReportInput.state`'s `Pick`.\n3. **Creation, atomic and rollback-safe.**\n   - A new `Store.createAcceptanceRun(repo, req, snapshot)` calls `insertRun` with the initial `state_json` in the same `INSERT`, inside `createRun`'s existing transaction (`store.ts:1220-1270`, including the issue claim check). `state_json` is added to that explicit column list.\n   - **A complete initial state.** Today the engine builds a new run's state inline in `RunContext` (`src/pipeline/context.ts:395-404`: `phase`, `answers`, `round`, `roundsOnImplementer`, `triedImplementers`, `feedback`, `toolCommands`) and uses a stored state wholesale.\n     - Factor those defaults into an exported `initialRunState(run)`. `RunContext` keeps calling it, with unchanged behaviour.\n     - `createAcceptanceRun` builds `{ ...initialRunState(run), flow: \"acceptance\", acceptance: { snapshot }, needsHumanReason: ACCEPTANCE_BLOCK, deliveryComplete: true }`. That is a complete `RunState` with round 0, then the acceptance fields and rollback guards, persisted atomically as below.\n     - `needsHumanReason` makes an older engine end the run needs_human on first pickup (the `REVIEW_RESOLUTION_BLOCK` pattern, `engine.ts:232-270`).\n     - `deliveryComplete: true` makes every release's `deliver` and `deliverVerifiedDraft` return without publishing (`engine.ts:2818`, `:3000`).\n     - Both are kept through every checkpoint.\n   - The new engine allows `ACCEPTANCE_BLOCK` only when `flow === \"acceptance\"`.\n   - The state is never accepted from a client. `CreateRunRequest` over HTTP can't carry it; only `createAcceptanceRun` writes it.\n   - **Trust check before writing.**\n     - A pure `acceptanceRunRequest({ ticket, parent, trusted })` requires the parent to exist, and the ticket and parent to pass the queue's trusted-author and trusted-editor test.\n     - Factor that test out of `issueEligibility` (`src/integrations/issue-queue.ts:61-137`) into one helper, used by both.\n     - Otherwise it throws with the reason, and no run is created.\n4. **Intent resolution,** after prepare pins the SHA and before any model call.\n   - **Where the units come from.** The source is the ticket's `## The original intent` section of the snapshot, as follows:\n     - **(a) Quoted units:** each blockquote paragraph (`\u003e …`), and each list item, in that section. The source is the nearest preceding line of the form `From #\u003cn\u003e…:` or `From \u003cpath\u003e…:`; with none, it's the parent.\n       - **Each quote must equal one whole unit of its source.** The source is the snapshotted body of the parent (#n must be the parent), or the file at the checked SHA (`readFileAt`, `src/git/repos.ts:494`, after `citedFileRefusal`).\n         - The source is split into units by the same splitter used for section references: list items, paragraphs, blockquote paragraphs and table cells. A blockquote containing a list contributes each item.\n         - List and quote markers are stripped and whitespace is normalized on both sides. The quote must then equal one unit's text exactly, never a substring.\n         - So `\u003e The service` quoting the start of a longer requirement is refused, as \"quote is not a whole source unit\".\n       - This covers #818 and #858 (blockquotes from the parent), #819 (blockquotes from #38 and docs/PLAN.md, plus the owner's decisions as list items from #38), and #857 (one blockquote from #821, which isn't the parent, so it is refused until the ticket names its source as the parent's section).\n     - **(b) Section references:** a line naming a quoted heading of the parent, as in #857 and #829: `#823's \"Epic D: defects become issues\" section`.\n       - Every list item and paragraph of that section is a unit, including nested subsections, up to the next heading of the same or a higher level. Code fences and `\u003cdetails\u003e` blocks are left out.\n       - A heading text that matches zero or more than one heading is refused.\n   - **Evidence class, from trusted grammar only.**\n     - Every unit is `behaviour` unless the ticket marks it `docs`: a `(docs)` suffix on its lead-in line (`From #784 (docs):`) or on its section reference (`#784's \"W4\" section (docs)`).\n     - The class is stored in the manifest with the unit. The model's schema has no class field, so its output can't set or change the class.\n   - **What isn't a unit.** Plain prose paragraphs in the section, such as \"In short: …\" or \"This check doesn't use it.\", are context, not units.\n   - **Mixed forms and duplicates.** Mixed forms take the union. Units are deduplicated by normalized text, and a quoted unit inside a referenced section is one unit.\n   - **The manifest.** Units are numbered `U1…Un` in order of first appearance. The manifest (ids, texts, evidence classes, sources and the SHA) is saved with `ctx.save` before the model is invoked.\n   - **Refusals.** An empty manifest, an unresolvable source, or a quote that isn't a whole source unit ends the run before any model call. The run is `failed`, with the reason.\n5. **Prepare.** In the acceptance flow, prepare does only this:\n   - fetch the default branch (`fetchBase`, `repos.ts:464`);\n   - record its head as the checked SHA;\n   - create a detached worktree there with `addDetachedWorktree` (`repos.ts:595-603`), with no branch allocation, PR lookup or baseline gates;\n   - read `gatesConfig` from that commit's `.limitless.toml`;\n   - run its `[gates] setup` once under gate confinement (`runLocalGates` with no checks, `src/gates/run.ts:225`, as the preview does), recording `setupDone`.\n\n   A setup failure ends the run `failed`, with the redacted setup output, before any model call.\n6. **The accept stage.**\n   - **Prompt:** `acceptancePrompt` (`src/pipeline/prompts.ts`), given the manifest and the ticket as quoted data. It is told to assess each unit as a whole.\n   - **Invocation:** the `verify` role, readonly with tools, in the detached worktree. No routing change.\n   - **Output:** a strict `AcceptanceSchema` (`src/pipeline/schemas.ts`), with one item per unit: `{ unit: \"U\u003cn\u003e\", verdict: met|partly_met|unmet|regressed|manual, files: [{ path, lines? }], tests: [{ file, name }], note }`. There is no class field. A `manual` verdict can only keep a unit from passing.\n   - **Checkpoint:** the parsed output is saved before any test runs. On resume, if it exists, the model isn't invoked again.\n7. **Engine checks and verdicts,** in a new `src/pipeline/acceptance.ts`.\n   - **Assessment count:**\n     - a unit with no item is `not_assessed`;\n     - a unit with two or more items is `unmet`, \"duplicate assessments\";\n     - an item naming an unknown unit is dropped.\n   - **Tests:** the cited tests of every item claiming `met` run through `runCoveringRequests` at the checked SHA, with a `checkHead` that requires the worktree head to still equal it. Each is accepted only if `coveringTestRefusal(record, sha, succeededCoveringStages(ctx))` returns nothing. Caps and their reasons are #915's.\n   - **Files:**\n     - Each cited file is accepted only if `citedFileRefusal` returns nothing.\n     - `lines`, when present, must lie within the file at the SHA.\n     - A file-only `met` stands only for a unit whose manifest class is `docs`, and only with at least one verified file matching the base `[gates] docs` globs (`globToRegex`). For a `behaviour` unit it becomes `unmet`: \"behaviour requirement needs a passing covering test\".\n   - **Verdict:** `met` stands only under the invariant; otherwise it becomes `unmet`, with the engine's first refusal reason.\n     - `manual` items (demos, live checks) are never `met`, and are listed for the orchestrator.\n     - `partly_met`, `unmet` and `regressed` stand as reported, with only verified citations kept.\n     - `note` is shown labelled \"model note (unverified)\" and never counts as evidence.\n   - **Report citations** are only engine-generated:\n     - for tests, #915's `coveringCitation` format (stage id, `file › name`, executed command);\n     - for files, `path@sha` with the line range.\n8. **Outcome and terminal handling,** before any generic error path.\n   - The outcome (per-unit verdicts and citations, refusals, `not_assessed`, `manual` and the SHA) is written once, to `RunState.acceptance.outcome` and an `acceptance.json` artifact, with a `## Acceptance` report section. On resume with an outcome saved, nothing is recomputed: this is the acceptance stage's own completed-outcome replay.\n   - **Statuses:**\n     - a pass: `succeeded`, with no PR;\n     - a non-pass: `needs_human`, with a summary such as \"3 met, 1 unmet, 1 not assessed, 1 manual\";\n     - a reader or setup failure: `failed`.\n   - For flow `acceptance`, `executeScopedRun`'s error handling never takes the draft-delivery branch (`engine.ts:495-512`). `deliveryComplete: true` independently guarantees that no release can publish.\n9. **No entry point in this slice.** Acceptance runs are created only through `createAcceptanceRun`, which P4a-2's entry points call. With no trigger, no build path can be bypassed yet, and P4a-2 adds the trigger together with every refusal.\n\n## Tests\nEach must fail without its change. Use the fake harness, a seeded fixture repository with real git, and #915's existing covering-test seams. Make no network calls.\n\n**Shared primitive**\n1. #915's verifier tests pass unchanged. In particular, `coveringTestCommand` returns the same reasons in the same order for `--` templates, untracked files, files outside the repository and invalid names.\n   - **Several invalid properties at once:**\n     - a request whose file is outside the repository, whose name has a control character, and which isn't tracked returns the containment reason, as today;\n     - one inside the repository that isn't a test file and isn't tracked returns \"file is not a test file\";\n     - one with a valid test file and an invalid name, untracked, returns \"invalid test name\".\n\n     In each case the reason is the same before and after the extraction.\n\n**Outcomes**\n\n2. **All met.** Every unit has a passing covering test. The run is `succeeded`, with no PR, branch or push in fake GitHub, and the report cites each stage.\n3. **Non-passes.** Unmet, manual and not-assessed outcomes each end `needs_human`, and a reader failure ends `failed`, all with no push or PR.\n\n**Evidence (adversarial)**\n\n4. A claimed `met` becomes `unmet` when its cited test fails, is skipped, matches no testcase, or has a stale or missing JUnit report (all #915 refusals); when its file is untracked or outside the repository; or when its line range is out of bounds.\n5. **Empty and file-only evidence:**\n   - `met` with no evidence is `unmet`;\n   - a behaviour unit citing files only is `unmet`;\n   - **behaviour claimed as docs:** for a `behaviour` unit (no `(docs)` marker), the model cites only an existing in-glob README and adds `\"class\": \"docs\"`. The strict schema rejects the extra field. Without it, the citation still leaves the unit `unmet`, \"behaviour requirement needs a passing covering test\";\n   - a `docs`-class unit (marked in the ticket) with `files: []` is `unmet`;\n   - a `docs`-class unit citing a file outside the docs globs is `unmet`;\n   - a `docs`-class unit with one in-glob file stays `met`.\n6. **Assessment count:**\n   - two items for one unit make it `unmet`;\n   - a missing item leaves the unit `not_assessed`, and the run can't pass;\n   - an unknown unit id is dropped;\n   - a \"verified by gate run 12\" note with no test is `unmet`.\n\n**Intent**\n\n7. **A #784-shaped parent body** (Goal, Why, Where things stand, Plan, Risks, Tracking) with a ticket blockquoting only the Goal and the demo: two units, and the Why and Risks bullets create none.\n8. **#819-shaped:** blockquotes from #38 and docs/PLAN.md, and decision bullets, resolve. A docs/PLAN.md quote not present at the SHA is refused before the model.\n9. **Whole-unit quotes:**\n   - `\u003e The service` quoting the start of a longer parent requirement is refused before the model;\n   - a quote equal to a whole list item, paragraph or PLAN.md table cell resolves;\n   - a blockquoted list resolves item by item;\n   - a `(docs)` lead-in marks exactly its units `docs`, and everything else stays `behaviour`.\n10. **Section references:**\n   - a section reference includes its nested subsections, and excludes code fences and `\u003cdetails\u003e`;\n   - an ambiguous heading is refused;\n   - a ticket with neither form, or an empty manifest, is refused;\n   - a quoted unit inside a referenced section is deduplicated.\n\n**Trust and creation**\n\n11. A parent edited by an untrusted account, a ticket with no parent, or an untrusted ticket author: no run is created.\n12. A run created by `createAcceptanceRun` has, in `state_json` from its first committed row, exactly `initialRunState(run)` (round 0, empty `answers`, `triedImplementers` and `toolCommands`, and the other defaults) plus the acceptance state, `ACCEPTANCE_BLOCK` and `deliveryComplete`. `RunContext` loads it with no default filled in afterwards. An HTTP `CreateRunRequest` can't set any of it.\n\n**Rollback (old-engine fixture)**\n\n13. The persisted state of three acceptance runs is run through the engine with the acceptance flow branch and the `ACCEPTANCE_BLOCK` allowance removed. That is the previous release's behaviour; the fixture uses a seam, and the orchestrator repeats the check once against the real previous release before landing. The three runs:\n    - never picked up;\n    - prepared, with a worktree;\n    - partially completed, with model output saved.\n\n    Each ends `needs_human`, with no `git push`, PR or comment in fake GitHub.\n\n**Restart and resume**\n\n14. **Crash boundaries:**\n    - after the manifest checkpoint, and after the model output checkpoint: no new model invocation;\n    - after one covering test's record: it isn't re-run;\n    - after the outcome is saved and before the status update: the status completes, with nothing recomputed.\n15. **Cancellation** during a covering run stops the test under #915's handling and ends `cancelled`, with no outcome.\n16. **Pinned SHA:** advancing the default branch mid-run changes neither the test SHA nor the reported SHA.\n\n## Compatibility\n- **Rollback:** requirement 3's persisted block and `deliveryComplete` make an older release end acceptance runs `needs_human` without publishing, from creation on (test 12). The new fields are optional, and `state_json` was already a column.\n- **Restart and resume:**\n  - manifest, model output and outcome are checkpointed;\n  - covering tests use #915's durable records;\n  - setup is recorded, and re-runs only if a crash came before it was recorded.\n- **Verifier behaviour** is unchanged (test 1).\n- **Polling only:** no webhook involvement in this slice.\n- **Config:** no new keys.\n- **Runs created before this change** are unaffected.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Entry points (queue label, CLI, webhook) and build-path refusals (P4a-2).\n- Follow-up issues, the two-pass bound, closing the epic, and comments (P4b).\n- Running demos, which stay `manual`.\n- A new routing role.\n- Normalizing the existing tickets (an orchestrator step before P4a-2's trigger is used).\n\n## Budget\nAbout 245 changed source lines plus tests:\n- shared primitive ~25;\n- types and state ~15;\n- creation and trust ~30;\n- prepare ~30;\n- intent resolution ~50;\n- stage, prompt and schema ~35;\n- checks and verdicts ~35;\n- outcome and terminal handling ~25.\n\nStop at 250 and report.\n\n---\n\n"
}
